hold-and-rework

Reason: the G.A-v2 idea is directionally useful, but the v1.1 spec is not file-ready. The main blockers are: required reference documents are missing from the checkout; the spec has no per-ticket boundaries / required paths even though the review prompt and G.A-v1 precedent require those at filing quality; several integration tickets are tier:S despite being integration / soak / migration gates; the SD-1 dog-food rule is introduced without evidence blocks for the spec's own novelty-style claims; and multiple recovery / rescue paths remain operator-shaped rather than deterministic enough to file.

## §1. P0 BLOCKING findings (must fix before file)

### P0-1 — Required review corpus is incomplete in this checkout

Evidence:
- Spec related block references ADR-0023, ADR-0033, ADR-0034, parent `sprint-s12g-governance-engine-spec.md`, and phase specs as dependencies (`docs/sprint-s12/sprint-s12g-A-v2-runtime-defense-contract-spec.md:7-14`).
- Spec says the new rules extend G.A-v0 forbidden combinations per `sprint-s12g-governance-engine-spec.md §0 P1` (`docs/sprint-s12/sprint-s12g-A-v2-runtime-defense-contract-spec.md:102-113`).
- Spec relies on ADR-0033 authority and ADR-0034 override lifecycle in the schema and bootstrap path (`docs/sprint-s12/sprint-s12g-A-v2-runtime-defense-contract-spec.md:94-99`, `389-390`).
- Local evidence: the required prompt paths `docs/sprint-s12/sprint-s12g-governance-engine-spec.md`, `docs/sop/sprint-s12-ticket-decomposition-rules.md`, and ADR-0023/0033/0034/0035 are not present in `git ls-files` or `find docs` in this checkout.

Impact: reviewers cannot verify whether G.A-v2 extends the parent governance model correctly, whether tickets comply with the Sprint S12 decomposition rules, or whether authority / override semantics match ADR-0033/0034/0035. Filing a child ticket from an unverifiable spec would bypass the very governance contract the spec is trying to add.

Concrete fix: add or restore the named parent spec, SOP, and ADR docs before filing, or amend §0/§6 to point to their actual repository paths. Include a short `review_corpus:` block in the spec with exact paths and commit SHAs for each required reference.

### P0-2 — SD-1 self-compliance fails: the spec creates `novelty-claim-requires-evidence` but contains no actual evidence block for its own trigger phrases

Evidence:
- SD-1 requires novelty phrases in ticket / ADR / architecture memo text to have an accompanying `evidence_grep_artifact` block (`docs/sprint-s12/sprint-s12g-A-v2-runtime-defense-contract-spec.md:115-147`).
- The spec's own text contains novelty-style claims: "5 new required fields" (`43`), "new combinations" (`307`), many "new" defense dimensions (`188`, `220`, `238`, `263`, `288`), and "NEW shared plumbing" (`390`).
- The only `evidence_grep_artifact` occurrences in the spec are the schema definition / examples, not evidence for the spec's own claims (`docs/sprint-s12/sprint-s12g-A-v2-runtime-defense-contract-spec.md:123-133`, `314`).
- The architecture memo that triggered SD-1 still contains corrected novelty claims with no machine-readable evidence block around the "actually new" 3-layer mapping (`docs/architecture/2026-05-14-runner-pivot-and-three-layer-architecture.md:135-148`).

Impact: even with the prompt's 4-week soft-fail note, this is a dog-food failure. If v2-A9 scans v2-A1..A7 and related architecture docs, it will either warn on the bootstrap spec itself or require exclusions broad enough to weaken SD-1.

Concrete fix: add a top-of-file `evidence_grep_artifact` block covering every intentional novelty claim, or narrow the SD-1 regex / exclusions so schema-evolution phrases like "new field" are explicitly outside scope. Also add evidence for the architecture memo's "3-layer mapping is new" claim or rephrase it as an operator decision rather than historical novelty.

