   374	
   375	### Family ⑥ — Image-vs-DB alembic head drift  ⚠ HIGHEST PRIORITY
   376	
   377	**Why highest priority**: this is the gap that produced today's outage; affects every prod restart; biggest design blind spot in S12 (S12 implicitly assumes drift is impossible).
   378	
   379	**Defense dimensions covered**: D1 (detection) ✓ partial → full; D2 (exception with remediation) → new; D3 (shutdown gate already via /readyz) ✓; D4 (recovery) → new; D5 (rescue) → new.
   380	
   381	**Architectural decision LOCKED (operator 2026-05-14, Q1)**: **Option C — asymmetric upgrade**
   382	
   383	- If `image_alembic_head > db_alembic_head` (image AHEAD): auto-run `alembic upgrade head` on container startup, idempotent.
   384	- If `image_alembic_head == db_alembic_head` (aligned): no-op.
   385	- If `image_alembic_head < db_alembic_head` (image BEHIND): **refuse to start**; container exit-code 78 (`EX_CONFIG`); structured log line + remediation hint pointing to newer image tag.
   386	- Rationale: rolled-back image must not advance the DB further, but a forward image must not silently run on a behind DB either. Option C makes drift impossible to mask: forward drift self-heals; backward drift is loud and operator-actionable.
   387	
   388	Rejected: Option A (auto-up always — rolled-back image advances DB, increases drift); Option B (always block — deploy script bug = hard outage).
   389	
