   142	
   143	### §3.4 L1-exclusive rule v2 (codex P0 refinement)
   144	
   145	L1-exclusive applies when ANY of:
   146	- `external_payload_class: key-material` AND `credential_custody: generate|rotate|destroy`
   147	- `external_side_effect: meta-closure`
   148	- `l1_exclusive_reason` explicitly set (must justify)
   149	- `authority_required: L1` explicitly set
   150	- ticket grants `persistent_authority` to another identity (e.g., adding to roster)
   151	- ticket touches `external_systems: DNS | billing | idp`
   152	- `reversibility: irreversible` AND `environment_scope: prod | release-infra`
   153	- ticket modifies release-signing policy (cosign key + release tag policy)
   154	- ticket performs `credential_custody: rotate|destroy` on production secrets
   155	
   156	Rule key: **authority persistence + blast radius + custody + irreversibility** (NOT just "key-material + system").
   157	
   158	### §3.5 L2 8-category reason taxonomy (codex P0)
   159	
   160	When `class: operator-window-deputy`, ticket MUST declare `l2_reason`:
   161	
   162	| l2_reason | Semantics |
   163	|---|---|
   164	| `execution-only` | Deputy executes a pre-approved runbook step; no new judgment |
   165	| `witness-only` | Deputy witnesses + records an operation (e.g., smoke test) |
   166	| `approval-only` | Deputy approves a runner-prepared artifact (e.g., deploy script) |
   167	| `credential-entry` | Deputy enters credentials at prompt (e.g., 31.A-2b operator-prompt) |
   168	| `production-touch` | Deputy interacts with prod systems within pre-approved scope |
   169	| `release-governance` | Deputy participates in release process (but NOT release tag itself — L1) |
   170	| `roster-mutation` | **NOT ALLOWED for L2** — roster mutations are L1-exclusive |
   171	| `override-action` | **NOT ALLOWED for L2** — override is L1-exclusive |
   172	| `destructive-action` | Deputy executes a destructive op within pre-defined bounded scope |
   173	
   174	Filing-hook rejects ticket if `class: operator-window-deputy` AND `l2_reason in [roster-mutation, override-action]`.
   175	
   176	### §3.6 L3 runner refusal contract v2 (codex P0)
   177	
   178	Runner pickup MUST refuse tickets per these precedence rules:
   179	1. If ANY `class:operator-window-*` label present → refuse (regardless of subscription-* also present)
   180	2. `pre_pickup_ok()` enforces authority class check (not just labels)

