    15	
    16	# Sprint S12 Bedrock — Ticket Decomposition Rules
    17	
    18	## §1. Why this document exists
    19	
    20	Sprint S12 (per ADR-0023) will produce **~250 tickets across 11 sub-phases over 18-26 weeks**. The previous wave (Sprint S0 "Foundation 2026-05-06") shipped ADR-0001 + ADR-0002 as documents but the implementation never landed; the result was 13 cross-cutting failures discovered 2026-05-13 (see ADR-0023 §1.1 + Appendix A).
    21	
    22	S0 vs S12 difference: S0 specified WHAT (architecture intent). S12 must specify HOW (executable contract). **A ticket whose AC could be misread by codex-cli, claude-cli, or a future operator IS a ticket that will be misread.**
    23	
    24	Specifically, the past 5 days of rescue work (2026-05-08 to 2026-05-13) surfaced **5 incident patterns** + **2 meta-patterns** that this document formalises into hard rules. Every Sprint S12 ticket spec MUST conform; OP-1042 (filing-time validation hook) enforces at filing time.
    25	
    26	This is not optional advice. It is the anchor that prevents Sprint S12 from becoming another Sprint S0.
    27	
    28	---
    29	
    30	## §2. Pattern 1 — Multi-area AC must reverse-audit area labels
    31	
    32	### 2.1 What goes wrong
    33	
    34	When an AC references a file path that's in an area the ticket doesn't declare, the runner enforces its area-boundary discipline and refuses to make the change. This produces a `[codex-blocked]: out-of-area dependency` revert. Examples observed:
    35	
    36	| Incident | AC referenced | Ticket areas | Result |
    37	|---|---|---|---|
    38	| OP-989 (29b Sprint F infra) | `docs/sop/3d-memory-architecture.md` | `area:devops, area:backend` | codex bail with out-of-area; ticket stuck for hours |
    39	| OP-1016 (29a-1 deployment audit baseline) | `docs/audit/2026-05-13-deployment-audit-baseline.md` | `area:devops, area:tooling` | same pattern; 4 revert cycles before operator unblocked |
    40	| OP-1029 (29d-1 Caddy) | docs/sop/cross-host-portability-staging.md | `area:devops` only | codex partial-complete + revert |
    41	
    42	Root cause: AC was written by humans in prose form; ticket labels were tagged separately. No automated check linked the two.
    43	
    44	### 2.2 The rule
    45	
    46	> **Filing-time validation hook (extends OP-1042)**: every ticket's AC text MUST be scanned for file path references. Each path maps to an `area:*` label per the table below. The ticket's label set MUST contain every implied area, OR the AC text MUST be rephrased to defer those changes to a child ticket. **Otherwise filing is rejected.**
    47	
    48	### 2.3 Path → area mapping (canonical)
    49	
    50	| Path prefix | Maps to area |
    51	|---|---|
    52	| `docs/`, `*.md` at repo root | `area:docs` |
    53	| `backend/`, `*.py` at repo root | `area:backend` |
    54	| `backend/tests/`, `tests/` | `area:tests` |
    55	| `app/`, `components/`, `hooks/`, `*.tsx`, `*.ts` (frontend) | `area:frontend` |
    56	| `deploy/systemd/`, `deploy/k8s/`, `deploy/helm/`, `*.service`, `*.timer`, `Dockerfile*`, `docker-compose*.yml` | `area:devops` |
    57	| `scripts/` (top-level), `*.sh`, `*.py` under `scripts/` | `area:tooling` |
    58	| `.gitlab-ci.yml`, `.github/workflows/*` | `area:ci` (NEW for Sprint S12) |
    59	| `backend/security/`, `backend/auth/`, `backend/credentials/`, cosign material | `area:security` |
    60	| `backend/alembic/`, `*.sql`, DB schemas | `area:db` |
    61	| `gerrit/`, Gerrit config | `area:gerrit` |
    62	| `.config/omnisight/*.env` (operator creds) | `area:devops + class:operator-prepare-only` |
    63	
    64	### 2.4 Enforcement implementation
    65	
    66	In `file_jira_ticket.py` `validate_areas_match_description()`:
    67	
    68	```python
    69	# Strict mode (Sprint S12+):
    70	def validate_areas_match_description_strict(areas: set[str], description_text: str) -> list[str]:
    71	    referenced = scan_paths_to_areas(description_text)
    72	    missing = referenced - areas
    73	    if not missing:
    74	        return []
    75	    # Sprint S12: hard reject (no --force escape)
    76	    raise ValidationError(
    77	        f"AC references paths in {sorted(missing)} but ticket labels only "
    78	        f"include {sorted(areas)}. Add labels OR split docs/tests changes into "
    79	        f"a child ticket. (Sprint S12 strict mode; see SOP-S12-TICKET-DECOMP §2)."
    80	    )
    81	```
    82	
    83	The OP-1042 (lint hook) implementation already has `is_canonical_label()`. Extend with this audit. Test cases: file synthetic tickets matching each rescue pattern from §2.1; assert filing rejected.
    84	
    85	### 2.5 Escape hatch
    86	
    87	A ticket may include AC referring to area X without label area:X **only if** the AC explicitly defers that work to a child:
    88	
    89	```markdown
    90	### 1. Code AC
    91	- [ ] `backend/agents/foo.py`: new function bar()
    92	- [ ] `docs/sop/foo-runbook.md` updated  ← deferred: see ticket OP-NNNN (area:docs child)
    93	```
    94	
    95	The hook recognises the literal pattern `deferred: see ticket OP-NNNN` and allows the AC to pass.
    96	
    97	---
    98	
    99	## §3. Pattern 2 — Sibling tickets need an Integration ticket
   100	
   101	### 3.1 What goes wrong
   102	
   103	Sibling tickets (same parent META, similar tier) each ship "their part" but the chain between them is never end-to-end-verified until production breaks. Examples:
   104	
   105	| Incident chain | Per-ticket status | Real outcome |
   106	|---|---|---|
   107	| OP-1015/1019/1026/1028 (Missing tree) | All 4 marked 公開済み individually | Push chain to Gerrit silently failed for 90+ min; 7 incidents back-to-back |
   108	| AUDIT-29 Phase 31.E migration (hypothetical) | 21 per-job migration tickets all green | Could ship 21 GitLab CI jobs that individually pass but collectively fail parity (artifact names diverged, required-check semantics drifted) |
   109	| OP-693 + OP-694 + OP-1042 (label hygiene cluster) | each shipped | Coordinator + lint-hook + schema doc; if no integration test the chain doesn't fire on a real malformed ticket |
   110	
   111	Root cause: 4-AC discipline (Code/Deploy/Integration/Exercised) is checked PER TICKET. But "Integration AC" of one ticket can be a false-positive when the integration spans multiple tickets.
   112	
   113	### 3.2 The rule
   114	
   115	> Every group of sibling sub-tickets (same parent META, doing related work) MUST have **one explicit `integration-*` ticket** that does ONLY the end-to-end verification of the group. The integration ticket:
   116	> - **tier:M or higher** (cannot be tier:S — integration scope is too holistic)
   117	> - blockedBy ALL siblings in the group
   118	> - parentMeta same as siblings
   119	> - AC focuses on: real chain execution + evidence + drift detection
   120	> - Closes the sibling group's parent sub-META gate
   121	
   122	### 3.3 What the integration ticket looks like
   123	
   124	For each sibling group, the integration ticket follows this template:
   125	
   126	```
   127	Title: integration-{group-name}: end-to-end verify {N} siblings + parity report
   128	Labels:
   129	  - tier:M (minimum)
   130	  - type:integration  (new label, distinguishes from feature/bug/cleanup)
   131	  - area:{union of sibling areas}
   132	  - capability:enable=run_tests (typically)
   133	  - class:subscription-{claude|codex} (prefer claude for verification work)
   134	parentMeta: <sibling parent>
   135	blockedBy: <ALL siblings>
   136	
   137	### Scope
   138	Run the {group-name} end-to-end chain in real environment + emit evidence
   139	file at `docs/audit/AUDIT-31-phase-{X}-evidence/integration-{group-name}.json`.
   140	
   141	### 1. Code AC
   142	- [ ] `tests/integration/test_{group-name}.py` exists
   143	- [ ] Test exercises the FULL chain (not mock); pytest exit 0
   144	  verify:
   145	    command: pytest tests/integration/test_{group-name}.py -v 2>&1
   146	    expect_exit_code: 0
   147	    expect_stdout_match: "PASSED.*test_{group-name}"
   148	    timeout_seconds: 600
   149	
   150	### 2. Deploy AC
   151	- [ ] All sibling artefacts (containers/scripts/services/yaml) deployed
   152	- [ ] systemctl/docker/file evidence per sibling captured in evidence JSON
   153	  verify:
   154	    command: scripts/sprint-s12-evidence-collect.sh phase-{X}
   155	    expect_exit_code: 0
   156	    expect_stdout_match: "evidence_complete: true"
   157	
   158	### 3. Integration AC
   159	- [ ] End-to-end real-traffic test (or scheduled job run with success signal)
   160	  verify:
   161	    command: scripts/run-integration-{group-name}.sh
   162	    expect_exit_code: 0
   163	
   164	### 4. Exercised AC
   165	- [ ] >=24h sustained green observation
   166	- [ ] No `[verify-failed]` events from any sibling's verify hook
   167	  verify:
   168	    command: jq '.failures' /var/log/sprint-s12/verify-events.jsonl | grep -c "{group-name}"
   169	    expect_stdout_match: "^0$"
   170	    expect_exit_code: 0
   171	
   172	### Go-Live target
   173	{T+1d after all siblings closed}
   174	```
   175	
   176	### 3.4 When to NOT have integration ticket
   177	
   178	A solo sub-ticket (no siblings, just one work-unit) doesn't need a separate integration ticket. The work-unit's own 4-AC Integration section is sufficient.
   179	
   180	But: **if you find yourself wanting to split a "do X" into 2+ sub-tickets, you must also create the integration ticket**. The split + integration is the unit, not the split alone.
   181	
   182	### 3.5 Anti-pattern: "We'll add the integration ticket later"
   183	
   184	This pattern was observed in AUDIT-29: tickets shipped, then a follow-up "verify" was deferred. The follow-up never happened because the parent META closed first. **The integration ticket goes in at filing time, blockedBy is enforced, parent META cannot close until integration ticket closes.**
   185	
   186	---
   187	
   188	## §4. Pattern 3 — AC verify blocks must be machine-executable
   189	
   190	### 4.1 What goes wrong
   191	
   192	AC bullets written in English prose ("tests pass", "service deployed", "alert fires") leave codex/claude to infer how to verify. Inferred verifications drift from reality. Examples:
   193	
   194	| Incident | AC bullet (English) | What codex actually did | Gap |
   195	|---|---|---|---|
   196	| OP-995 (29h auto-archive) | "Bridge transitions 公開済み → Archived after retention window" | Wrote function code; ran 1 unit test on synthetic data | Never verified the real bridge daemon picked up new code path |
   197	| OP-1015/1019/1026 Missing tree | "Push to Gerrit refs/for/develop" | Ran `git push`; got "Missing tree" stderr; misread as race | No post-push verify (e.g., `gerrit query change-id` to confirm change exists) |
   198	| OP-1029 Caddy path-rule | "Caddy reloaded with new config" | Wrote config file; reloaded service | Never `curl`'d the path to verify routing actually changed |
   199	
   200	Root cause: ACs were not given exact verification commands; runners filled the gap with their own judgment which was insufficient.
   201	
   202	### 4.2 The rule
   203	
   204	> Every AC bullet that has a runtime expectation MUST include a `verify:` block. Filing-time hook rejects tickets where any AC bullet lacks `verify:` (except `verify: deferred-to-operator` explicit waiver).
   205	
   206	### 4.3 Verify block schema
   207	
   208	```yaml
   209	verify:
   210	  command: <shell command, must be runnable in the runner's CWD>
   211	  expect_exit_code: <integer, default 0>
   212	  expect_stdout_match: <regex OR exact string OR jsonpath-with-expected-value>
   213	  expect_stderr_absent: <regex of stderr that should NOT appear; optional>
   214	  timeout_seconds: <integer, default 60>
   215	  run_as: <runner | operator | runner-then-operator; default runner>
   216	```
