    11	
    12	# ADR-0033 — Governance Engine + Operator Authority Hierarchy
    13	
    14	## Status
    15	
    16	Proposed (2026-05-13).
    17	
    18	## Context
    19	
    20	Sprint S12: Bedrock (11 phases, ~306 tickets) consistently references **OP-1042 filing-time hook** to enforce ticket-level governance rules. Over the course of writing 11 phase specs, OP-1042 has accreted 12+ rule categories:
    21	
    22	1. boundary-schema validation (10+ fields per ticket)
    23	2. context_hint preamble (6 lines) for all tier:S tickets
    24	3. path canonicalization (e.g., GitLab lowercase per L-OP-247)
    25	4. key-material class enforcement (operator-* required when handling cryptographic keys)
    26	5. mixed-scope `scope_components` validation
    27	6. dynamic-ticket preflight (31.I-7-Template filing-script local validation)
    28	7. semantic blocker audit (31.J-ReadinessGate checks specific evidence fields per phase, not just status)
    29	8. jira-write / jira-read / meta-closure side-effect classification
    30	9. cross-phase blocker JQL preflight (verify prior phase Closed + commit SHA)
    31	10. tag_type: annotated enforcement
    32	11. repo-content-delete vs git-ref-rewrite distinction
    33	12. secret-leak patterns in CI YAML
    34	
    35	Per codex's cross-phase review (Q3d 2026-05-13):
    36	> "OP-1042 has grown from schema validation into a policy engine. It needs versioned schema modules and fixture tests per phase. Without that, OP-1042 becomes a silent single point of governance failure."
    37	
    38	Concurrently, **operator availability** has emerged as the single biggest schedule risk:
    39	- 11 phases × ~7 operator-window tickets = ~75 operator-touch events
    40	- Concentrated on a single human operator (sora) for "highest-stakes" decisions
    41	- Cutover sessions (31.J 5-step) require unbroken 2-4 hours
    42	- Some tickets are operationally simple but currently require top-tier operator authority (e.g., 31.D per-ref replication enablement)
    43	
    44	Operator's directive (2026-05-13):
    45	> "讓 副操作員具有僅次於最高權限的等級，必要時可直接代行。除非是最高級別任務須由操作員指示或動作，不然可以有條件的向下授權。"
    46	
    47	This requires a **3-level authority hierarchy** baked into the ticket schema, enforced by OP-1042.
    48	
    49	## Decision
    50	
    51	### 1. Extract OP-1042 from a single ticket into Sprint S12.G: Governance Engine
    52	
    53	OP-1042 is too complex for a single ticket; it's effectively a **policy engine**. Sprint S12.G (sibling to S12: Bedrock) implements it across 6 sub-phases:
    54	
    55	| Sub-phase | Scope |
    56	|---|---|
    57	| **G.A** | Canonical ticket-contract schema models (Pydantic + JSON Schema); covers all v2 boundary fields |
